# Copy to .env (or .env.local) and adjust for how you're running the app.
# Expo automatically loads EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars from this file — no extra
# tooling needed. app.config.ts falls back to the production URL baked into
# app.json's extra.apiBaseUrl if this var isn't set at all, so this file only
# needs to be populated when you want to point at something else.

# ============================================
# LOCAL DEV — against `docker compose up` in the repo root
# ============================================
# Caddy publishes host ports 80/443 on every interface (0.0.0.0), not just
# loopback — so it's reachable from a phone on the same Wi-Fi/LAN with no
# extra setup, the same way it's reachable from this PC's browser or an
# Android emulator. Find your machine's LAN IP with `ip route get 1.1.1.1`
# (Linux/macOS) — it can change between networks/DHCP renewals, so re-check
# it if requests suddenly start failing.

# Physical device on the same Wi-Fi/LAN as this machine (also works from a
# browser or Android emulator running on this same machine):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://<your-machine-LAN-ip>/api

# Equivalent alternatives if you'd rather not depend on the LAN IP:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost/api      # iOS Simulator / this PC's browser only
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2/api        # Android Emulator only

# If you ever need the dev stack NOT reachable from the LAN, bind caddy's
# ports to 127.0.0.1 in docker-compose.yml (or a personal, gitignored
# docker-compose.local.yml + `COMPOSE_FILE=...` in your root .env) and use a
# tunnel (e.g. `ngrok http 80`) for phone testing instead.

# ============================================
# PRODUCTION (default — matches app.json's extra.apiBaseUrl)
# ============================================
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://attendixv2.talenciaglobal.com/api

# ============================================
# EAS Build / CI (see eas.json + .github/workflows/mobile-release.yml)
# ============================================
# Not read from this file — EAS injects EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL per build
# profile via eas.json's build.<profile>.env, and CI needs an EXPO_TOKEN
# secret (from https://expo.dev/accounts/[account]/settings/access-tokens)
# to authenticate non-interactively. Neither belongs in a local .env.
